cl builds an array member of class type through the CRT's helpers and cxx1
builds the loop itself: ??_H, the vector constructor iterator, and ??_FM@@,
M's default constructor closure that the iterator calls once per element.
Neither is an ABI name - nothing outside the object refers to them, and the
cases run and agree - but cl has two symbols here that cxx1 does not.

Measured with cl on the Windows box, and worth saying how it was missed: the
case's .nonames claimed "the Windows comparison has one name per constructor
and no cleanup, and it agrees exactly". That claim was made from clang's
x86_64-pc-windows-msvc output by an agent that had no access to the box.
clang does not use ??_H; cl does. This is what cl-is-the-primary-oracle is
for, and the sentence has been corrected.
